<!--Post: 10958--><!--Time: 1110317842-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10958"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 1:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dennis Rader is an &#34;at home&#34; killer ... that much is evident.  He isn&#39;t one who travels the road and kills along the way.  He is familiar with the community he lives in and murders there.  So the police will probably be concerned with four time zones of unsolved cases. <BR> <BR>1.  1945-1966  Though he was not killing in his baby years there is no telling what happened during his highschool years.  Any murders in the area at this time will be looked into.  However if the family went on vacation then there should be a look into those areas, but I don&#39;t believe DR kills outside his nest.  The Hendersons is a prime example of a case during this era. <BR> <BR>2. 1966-1970 Not only do we have to worry about when he comes home for a short time, but these Japanese areas need to be looked into as well as any military deaths.  These places becomes home for a soldier. <BR> <BR>3. 1970-1991 All murders in the area need to be looked at, and I doubt these murders would be part of any plea agreement.  If BTK is fingered for the crime then it just means another life sentence.  There would be no point to hold out on this information, and DR wants people to know what he has done.  Vacationing at the time does not need to be looked at as closely, though it should still be considered anyway. <BR> <BR>4. 1991-2005 Any murders here are important, and DR knows it.  DR cares for his family, and his life.  This is a man with two personalities.  One of them I&#39;m sure does not want to die.  I can see DR holding out on information in this time period. Vacationing during this time period needs to be looked at a bit closer.  Though i doubt he would murder while on vacation, his kids are now living far from him and he may be comfortable enough in their hometowns to commit murder.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
