<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11263"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 5:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Emb, Donna Jabara Baker was the landlord, here are acouple of article snippits <BR> <BR>Source: Nickie Flynn, The Wichita Eagle <BR>The wife of a man convicted this week of murdering a Wichita woman was found guilty of forgery in Sedgwick County District Court on Thursday.Sherri Olin Kingsley, 25, was charged, pleaded guilty and was sentenced to 1 to 5 years in prison. Sherri Kingsley, who testified against her husband, Alan Kingsley, 23, admitted that she endorsed a $500 check that her husband had stolen from their landlady, Donna Jabara Baker, who was murdered in her Eastborough home on April 22.A jury this week  <BR> <BR>Published on August 30, 1991, Page 1D, Wichita Eagle, The &#40;KS&#41;  <BR> <BR>  <BR>Article 5 of 25; 640 words <BR> <BR> <BR>JURY FINDS KINGSLEY GUILTY OF MURDER <BR> <BR>Source: Nickie Flynn, The Wichita Eagle <BR>Alan Kingsley cried for himself Tuesday when a jury found him guilty of killing a Wichita woman, and then recommended a 40-year, no-parole sentence.The six-man, six-woman jury deliberated three hours before returning guilty verdicts on all five counts associated with the death of Donna Jabara Baker on April 22. Jurors took even less time, 39 minutes, to decide to recommend the &#34;hard-40&#34; sentence for Kingsley.Wichita businesswoman Helen Galloway, who has shed many tears over  <BR> <BR>Published on August 28, 1991, Page 1D, Wichita Eagle, The &#40;KS&#41;  <BR> <BR>this link is my search of kansas.com archives result page, may or may not work <BR><a href="http://nl.newsbank.com/nl-search/we/Archives?s_site=kansas&amp;p_multi=WE" target=_top>http://nl.newsbank.com/nl-search/we/Archives?s_sit e=kansas&amp;p_multi=WE</a>|&amp;p_product=WE&amp;p_theme=realcities&amp;p_action=search&amp; p_maxdocs=200&amp;p_text_search-0=donna%20AND%20jabara %20AND%20baker&amp;s_dispstring=donna%20jabara%20baker %20AND%20date&#40;01/04/1991%20to%2002/04/1992&#41;&amp;p_fiel d_date-0=YMD_date&amp;p_params_date-0=date:B,E&amp;p_text_ date-0=01/04/1991%20to%2002/04/1992&amp;p_perpage=10&amp;p _sort=YMD_date:D&amp;xcal_useweights=no<!--/Text--></td></tr>
